WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:09.739
"I hope Alpha is able to scan Sandville for other alien life-forms," Ally thought, racing into the house.

2
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.505
"I need to find out if Melanie is from Earth—or another galaxy!"

3
00:00:14.506 --> 00:00:21.007
"Ally!" Mateo hurried toward her, smiling from ear to ear. "I've got big news!"

4
00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:26.029
"Did you find me a less expensive plane ticket?" Ally asked hopefully.

5
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:29.423
"Sorry, not yet," Mateo said.

6
00:00:29.424 --> 00:00:34.936
"But I did find out that UserPFM5 lives in Sandville.

7
00:00:34.937 --> 00:00:37.947
I'm trying to figure out the person's real name.

8
00:00:37.948 --> 00:00:45.372
When I do, I'm going to ask UserPFM5 to sell the Cosmic Quest comic to me."

9
00:00:45.373 --> 00:00:50.325
"Someone else's real identity has to be figured out," Ally mumbled.

10
00:00:50.326 --> 00:00:54.582
Mateo looked confused. "What do you mean?"

11
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:57.334
"Nothing." Ally shook her head.

12
00:00:57.335 --> 00:01:02.389
"I don't want to bother Mateo with my suspicions about Melanie yet," she thought.

13
00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.478
"He has enough on his mind."

14
00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:07.982
"That sounds like a good plan," she said.

15
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:11.077
"I have to go check on Alpha right now."

16
00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:17.084
"Oh! Maybe later she can help me figure out who UserPFM5 is," Mateo said.

17
00:01:17.085 --> 00:01:21.606
Ally nodded. "Sure. We can try it."

18
00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:24.935
When Ally entered her room, Alpha's screen was lit.

19
00:01:24.936 --> 00:01:30.526
"Greetings, Allyzooba. Alpha reporting for duty. All systems go."

20
00:01:30.527 --> 00:01:33.999
"Yes!" Ally cheered.

21
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.262
"You're working—at last! And I have another job for you.

22
00:01:39.263 --> 00:01:43.966
I need you to scan Sandville for other alien life-forms."

23
00:01:43.967 --> 00:01:47.327
"Affirmative." Alpha's screen blinked once.

24
00:01:47.328 --> 00:01:50.594
"Alien life-form located in the park."

25
00:01:50.595 --> 00:01:55.655
Ally's heart pounded. "Show me on the screen, please."

26
00:01:55.656 --> 00:01:57.747
A live feed of the park appeared.

27
00:01:57.748 --> 00:02:01.510
There were people walking, Rollerblading, and picnicking.

28
00:02:01.511 --> 00:02:07.255
Ally spotted Phil and Tina chatting on a bench, but there was no sign of Melanie's purple hair.

29
00:02:07.256 --> 00:02:12.009
Suddenly Alpha zoomed in on a rock near the bench where Phil and Tina were sitting.

30
00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:18.580
"Detected: remnants of a comet that broke up approximately five hundred Earth years ago."

31
00:02:18.581 --> 00:02:23.258
"A rock?" Ally's eyes went wide.

32
00:02:23.259 --> 00:02:26.239
"Are you sure that's the alien life-form?"

33
00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:34.488
Alpha frowned. "Certainty is only at 85 percent because of the primitive Earth technology that I am housed in."

34
00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:38.491
"I'll take 85 percent!" Ally wiped her brow.

35
00:02:38.492 --> 00:02:43.730
"Phew! I guess Melanie is as human as everyone else in town.

36
00:02:43.731 --> 00:02:46.825
Okay, back to my other problem.

37
00:02:46.826 --> 00:02:53.494
You were going to figure out how to get me to Patagonia for a lot less than two thousand dollars." "Understood."

38
00:02:53.495 --> 00:02:55.622
Alpha blinked. "Lainie

39
00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:58.982
Polk is currently involved in a study of penguins in—" "I

40
00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:02.693
don't want to hear about her!" Ally covered her ears. "I

41
00:03:02.694 --> 00:03:06.588
need to figure out a way to get to Patagonia, otherwise I won't—" "Allyzooba!"

42
00:03:06.589 --> 00:03:09.019
Alpha snapped. "You

43
00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:14.583
are acting as impatient as an Earthling. Polk's research is in Patagonia." "It

44
00:03:14.584 --> 00:03:19.748
is?" Ally bit her lip. "That's a funny coincidence." "There

45
00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:24.678
is nothing humorous about it. Polk owns five private jets." "That's

46
00:03:24.679 --> 00:03:28.915
nice for her, if a bit much," Ally said. "You

47
00:03:28.916 --> 00:03:32.344
are not computing. She owes you a favor. Ask

48
00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:35.327
her to fly you to Patagonia." "Alpha,

49
00:03:35.328 --> 00:03:40.754
you're a genius!" Ally threw her arms around Alpha. Beep!

50
00:03:40.755 --> 00:03:44.028
Beep! "Allyzooba!" Alpha snapped. "That

51
00:03:44.029 --> 00:03:48.140
is not appropriate behavior! Unhand me!" "Fine."

52
00:03:48.141 --> 00:03:51.172
Ally backed away. "I'll

53
00:03:51.173 --> 00:03:53.839
just say thank you then." "That

54
00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.498
is acceptable." ***

55
00:03:56.499 --> 00:03:59.676
Ally dialed Lainie Polk's office.

56
00:03:59.677 --> 00:04:05.617
"Hi, this is Ally. Can you connect me to Lainie, please?" Ally asked.

57
00:04:05.618 --> 00:04:09.697
"Hi, Ally. She's difficult to reach," the assistant said.

58
00:04:09.698 --> 00:04:13.520
"In fact, you're the one who's responsible for her latest project.

59
00:04:13.521 --> 00:04:19.160
After she went to Sandville, she got very involved in saving different bird species.

60
00:04:19.161 --> 00:04:24.834
Currently she's in Patagonia working to save the habitat of the penguins."

61
00:04:24.835 --> 00:04:27.654
"Yes, I heard about that," Ally said.

62
00:04:27.655 --> 00:04:32.003
"That's why I'm calling. I would love to know more about her research."

63
00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:36.726
"I'm sure she'll be happy to tell you about it when she's back," the assistant said.

64
00:04:36.727 --> 00:04:39.023
"She's due back next fall."

65
00:04:39.024 --> 00:04:42.449
"What?" Ally almost shrieked into the phone.

66
00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.844
"Oh, well, uh, I can't wait that long!

67
00:04:45.845 --> 00:04:49.369
I'd really like to see it for myself—and soon!"

68
00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.086
"You want to go to Patagonia?"

69
00:04:52.087 --> 00:04:54.583
"I sure do!" Ally said.

70
00:04:54.584 --> 00:04:59.893
"Well, I'll get a message to her and see what she thinks," the assistant said.

71
00:04:59.894 --> 00:05:01.895
"When would you want to go?"

72
00:05:01.896 --> 00:05:04.597
"In a couple of days," Ally said.

73
00:05:04.598 --> 00:05:07.849
"Oh!" The assistant sounded surprised.

74
00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:13.012
"That's very soon. Then again, she does owe you an adventure.

75
00:05:13.013 --> 00:05:15.423
Let me try to get in touch with her.

76
00:05:15.424 --> 00:05:18.192
I'll call you back when I have an answer."

77
00:05:18.193 --> 00:05:23.537
"Thank you." Ally hung up and crossed her fingers on both hands.

78
00:05:23.538 --> 00:05:26.930
"Oh please, Lainie," she whispered.

79
00:05:26.931 --> 00:05:30.954
"You're my only hope!"

